Here is the commit message:
Allow 16M send/recv blocks

Fix an off by one error introduced by fcff0f3 which triggers an
assertion when 16M blocks are used with send/recv.  This fix was
intentionally not folder in to the Illumos commit so it can be
easily cherry-picked by upstream.

Signed-off-by: Brian Behlendorf <behlendorf1@llnl.gov>

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by an off-by-one error in the assertion that checked the size of the item being enqueued. The original assertion used a strict less-than comparison, which did not allow for the maximum size (16M) to be accepted, leading to an assertion failure when attempting to enqueue an item of that size.

